      {
        "id": "the-whole-disaster-started-with-a-cold-start-rattle",
        "title": "The whole disaster started with a cold-start rattle.",
        "description": "The rattle lasted only 1-2 seconds at first, then quietened. The owner assumed it was normal for a diesel. By 90,000 miles, the chain had snapped.",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "/case-studies/assets/1.2-bmw-n47-quote-comparison.png",
            "alt": "BMW N47 repair cost comparison - dealer £7,000+ versus specialist rebuild £2,800",
            "width": "",
            "height": ""
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "What owner thought"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "“Probably fine for a diesel”"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The car still drove normally, so the symptom did not feel urgent."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "What it actually was"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Tensioner failing"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The N47 tensioner was losing pressure, allowing the chain to stretch and slap."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Why it matters"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Snapped chain = bent valves"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Once the chain snaps, valves bend, rockers break, and the top end is destroyed."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "If your N47 rattles on cold start, book a timing chain inspection within 7 days. Do not wait for the chain to snap."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Failure timeline"
          }
        ],
        "links": [],
        "source": {
          "sectionId": "the-whole-disaster-started-with-a-cold-start-rattle",
          "order": 1
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "from-cold-start-rattle-to-snapped-chain-in-just-5-000-miles",
        "title": "From cold-start rattle to snapped chain in just 5,000 miles.",
        "description": "This case is a classic catastrophic N47 timing-chain failure: the owner ignored the warning signs and paid the price.",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "/case-studies/assets/2.2-bmw-n47-timeline.png",
            "alt": "BMW N47 timeline from rattle to snapped chain and dealer vs specialist quotes",
            "width": "",
            "height": ""
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "What the owner noticed"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "A cold-start rattle became a loud metallic snap at 30mph within 5,000 miles."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "What was happening internally"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The tensioner failed, the chain stretched and snapped, causing valve-to-piston contact and destroying the top end."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "“The dealer made it sound like the engine was a write-off. The independent specialist said, ‘Look, the bottom end is fine. The pistons aren’t damaged. We can rebuild the top end for a fraction of what a new engine costs.’ I saved over £4,000. Never again will I accept a dealer’s first quote for an engine replacement.”"
          },
